      "details": {
        "outcome": "passed",
        "review": "Seven footprint cells each need a base cube. Left requires three height-three stacks in distinct rows. Front allows that height only in its third column, forcing two extra cubes at each of the three rightmost cells. Front columns one and two also need an extra cube each. The lower bound is 7+6+2=15 and the height map 103 / 013 / 223 attains it. The offered nineteen exceeds even the maximum of seventeen. Fourteen misses one required peak and seventeen is achievable above the minimum."
      },
